## COMMUNICATION
Here we are reporting the porous metal-helix frameworks from the short \(\mathfrak{a},\gamma\cdot\) -hybrid peptide foldamers terminated by the metal coordinating bis(pyridyl) ligands and silver ions. These results suggest that helical foldamers can be used as templates to design new metal-helix frameworks.
